# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.
# Note: the `prisma` CLI (migrate/studio) reads a plain `.env` file, not
# `.env.local` - either duplicate DATABASE_URL into a root `.env`, or just
# run `npx prisma migrate dev` with DATABASE_URL set directly in your shell.

# Postgres connection string. Any Postgres works; a free one (e.g. Neon,
# neon.tech) is enough for development. Must include ?sslmode=require for
# most hosted providers.
DATABASE_URL=

# Anthropic API key used by app/api/chat/route.ts to talk to Claude.
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only needed if your ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is an org-wide key that isn't tied to
# a specific workspace (Anthropic will return an error asking for this if
# so). Find the workspace id in the Console URL while viewing that workspace,
# e.g. console.anthropic.com/workspaces/<this-part>/... , or leave unset if
# your key already works without it.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=

# Random secret used to encrypt the httpOnly session cookie that identifies
# the logged-in user (iron-session / AES-256-GCM). Must be at least 32
# characters. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional. Overrides the Claude model used for chat. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Optional. Overrides the Meta Graph API version used by the MCP server.
# Defaults to v22.0.
# META_GRAPH_API_VERSION=v22.0

# There is no Meta app ID/secret and no per-user access token here: the old
# MVP flow where each client manually pasted their own token is gone
# (Phase C - see AGENTS.md). Every user's Meta calls go through the one
# shared token below instead.

# The ONE Meta access token used for every Meta API call, for every client,
# across the whole app (see lib/adAccountAccess.ts). This is a Business
# Manager System User token - non-expiring, generated ONCE by the agency
# owner in Meta Business Settings (Business Settings > Users > System Users
# > [the system user] > Generate New Token, with ads_management /
# ads_read permissions and access to every client ad account shared with
# advertise4me's Business Portfolio). Required - Meta API calls fail with a
# clear error if this is unset, rather than crashing obscurely.
META_SYSTEM_USER_TOKEN=

# Transactional email (change-email verification, password reset, weekly
# summary, and account alerts - see lib/resend.ts). Get a key at
# https://resend.com/api-keys. If unset, email sends no-op with a console
# warning instead of crashing - fine during development, just set this
# before relying on any of the Settings email features in production.
RESEND_API_KEY=
